  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Europees burgerschap in de klas (2022), published by Leuven University Press, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 1,994 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Europees burgerschap in de klas by Griet Galle and Kris Grimonprez was published by Leuven University Press in 2022. Conceptually, the work connects to Humanities, Art, Political science, Theology and Philosophy.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,994 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Peace, Justice and strong institutions among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven, College of Europe and Fonds Lenaerts-Grimonprez.</p>",
